@* An explicit answer to "is there anything in this section?", in place of the switch that used to
   ask it.

   The switch was bound to the inverse of the flag it set, so the member read "I have nothing to
   declare" beside a control that was off -- off meaning that sentence was true. Which way round it
   went could only be worked out by flicking it, and because it started on "nothing", a section
   somebody never looked at was silently declared empty.

   Two buttons and nothing chosen: the question is asked in words, both answers are offered in
   words, and the member has to give one. Same pattern as the Insider declaration's NIN question,
   so the two declarations ask a yes/no the same way. *@

<div class="cg-declare-choice @(Value is null ? "is-unanswered" : "")">
    <p class="cg-declare-question" id="@_questionId">@Question</p>
    <div class="cg-yesno" role="group" aria-labelledby="@_questionId">
        <button type="button" class="cg-action-btn @(Value == false ? "cg-good" : "")"
                aria-pressed="@((Value == false).ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
                disabled="@Disabled" @onclick="() => SetAsync(false)">@YesLabel</button>
        <button type="button" class="cg-action-btn @(Value == true ? "cg-good" : "")"
                aria-pressed="@((Value == true).ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
                disabled="@Disabled" @onclick="() => SetAsync(true)">@NoLabel</button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>null until the member answers. true means "nothing to declare here".</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool? Value { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Question { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public string YesLabel { get; set; } = "Yes — I'll list them below";
    [Parameter] public string NoLabel { get; set; } = "No — nothing to declare";
    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    private readonly string _questionId = $"cg-declare-{Guid.NewGuid():N}";

    private Task SetAsync(bool nothingToDeclare) => ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(nothingToDeclare);
}
